// The Bay Loop (docs/SCENARIOS.md, docs/LAYOUTS.md): the Bay Area of the 2000s from the
// Golden Gate to the South Bay foothills, on its real ground and main roads. The city on
// its crests at the north-west, the red bridge to the headlands and the headlands road
// round to the East Bay; the bay bridge across; the Peninsula's ridge, foothill freeway,
// strip and bayshore freeway south to the flat South Bay and the foothill village; the
// bridges across the bay's south end.
//
// The sections between `realmap` markers are generated from public-domain US Census
// TIGER/Line 2023 roads and USGS 3DEP elevation by `tools/realmap` (import:
// tools/realmap/bay_loop.ron); edit that file and rerun it, not these sections. Road names
// are invented.
//
// Meters, x east, z south, (0, 0) the north-west corner; 32 x 32 chunks, 4096 m square.
